course: dictionary
lesson: 11892
title: Broadly
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Broadly is an adverb, a word that tells you how something is done. It has three main meanings, and the sentence around it tells you which one to use. Look for clues before you choose.
explain: First, broadly can mean in a general way, without all the details: «Broadly speaking, the plan is good.» The writer is giving the big idea, not every small part.
explain: Second, broadly can mean widely and openly: «Sam grinned broadly when he opened his present.» A broad grin is a big, wide smile that shows how happy Sam is.
explain: Third, broadly can mean mostly or on the whole: «I broadly agree with you.» You agree with most of what the other person says, but maybe not every single point.
fact: Broadly means in a general way, widely, or mostly.
fact: «Broadly speaking» means roughly, leaving out the small details.
fact: «Grinned broadly» means smiled with a big, wide smile.
fact: In science and maths reports, broadly often means roughly or in general.
fact: A quick check: swap in «generally» or «mostly». If the sentence still makes sense, you have probably found the right meaning.
exercise: «Broadly speaking, the plan is good.» What does broadly mean here? | *In a general way, without all the details | Only just | Very loudly | Wide and open, like a field
exercise: «The shy girl grinned broadly when she won.» What does broadly mean here? | Crossly | Very slowly | *With a big, wide smile | Quietly and secretly
exercise: «I broadly agree with the idea.» What does broadly mean here? | Not at all | *Mostly, on the whole | Angrily | Completely, with no doubt at all
test: «The two houses are broadly similar.» What does broadly similar mean? | Completely different | Exactly the same in every detail | *Alike in most ways | Shiny and new
test: Which word could replace broadly in «He smiled broadly»? | *Widely | Quietly | Sadly | Rarely
exam: «Broadly speaking, the story is about friendship.» Which word best fits the meaning of broadly? | *Generally | Angrily | Carefully | Loudly
